## ❓ Frequently Asked Questions

**Q: Is this safe to use?**
A: The layer operates externally and does not alter the game image on disk. It does, however, execute translated code, so a mismatch between your game build and the layer build is the most common crash source.

**Q: How do I uninstall it?**
A: Simply close the overlay and delete the folder. No system files are modified.

**Q: What is the difference between this and a plain emulator?**
A: A plain emulator only translates instructions. This package adds the reverse-engineering notes, the asset pipeline, and the port layer — input, pacing, config, and patch notes — so the result is playable instead of bootable.

